// Room 1: Millhaven PD front desk
#message 1 "Millhaven Police Department, 7:58 a.m. Officer Dana Reyes reports for her first week on patrol. Sergeant Prakash sits behind the front desk, sorting forms into three trays."
#message 2 "The front desk of the Millhaven Police Department. Sergeant Prakash works behind the counter under green fluorescent lights. A bulletin board hangs on the back wall. The records office is down the hall to the west. Glass doors lead east to Main Street."
#message 3 "Sergeant Prakash has twenty-two years on the force and a mustache that has outlasted three chiefs. He stamps forms without looking at them."
#message 4 "\"Reyes. Hale's Pharmacy on Main Street was broken into overnight. Somebody took a case of prescription painkillers.\""
#message 5 "\"A delivery driver, Marty Voss, called it in at 2:15 this morning. Says he saw the whole thing. He's waiting by his van on Main Street. Take his statement.\""
#message 6 "\"Then document the scene. Photographs, and anything the thief left behind.\" He slides a department camera across the counter. \"Bukowski is riding with you. He's out at the car. Try to keep him on topic.\""
#message 7 "\"The details are on the board if you forget. Dismissed.\""
#message 8 "\"Talk to the driver on Main Street. People remember things wrong. Check his story against something written down.\""
#message 9 "\"Hale's Pharmacy. Photograph the scene and bag anything the thief left behind. Talk to the pharmacist.\""
#message 10 "\"You've got a driver whose story doesn't hold and evidence from the scene. Records can tell you who rents what on Pier Road. Put it together.\""
#message 11 "\"You know where this goes. Radio dispatch for backup before you set foot in that warehouse. That's not advice, Reyes.\""
#message 12 "\"Write up the report, sign it and give it to me. Evidence attached.\""
#message 13 "\"Go home, Reyes. Come back tomorrow and do it again.\""
#message 14 "Wanted posters, a softball sign-up sheet and a typed notice: DAY SHIFT SEE SGT. PRAKASH FOR ASSIGNMENTS. The yellow index card in the middle is blank."
#message 15 "The yellow card reads: HALE'S PHARMACY, MAIN ST. BREAK-IN APPROX. 2 A.M. REPORTED 2:15 A.M. BY MARTY VOSS, QUICKLINE DELIVERY. TAKE STATEMENT. DOCUMENT SCENE."
#message 16 "Three wire trays sit on the counter, labeled IN, OUT and WRONG TRAY. The third one is the fullest."
#message 17 "\"Forms filed in the wrong tray go in that tray. Then I move them to the right tray. It's a system, Reyes.\""
#message 18 "Badge 417. The shine is still new."
#message 19 "Your handheld radio, set to channel two. Dispatch is on the other end."
#message 20 "Dispatch: \"Reyes, the sergeant is twenty feet away from you. Ask him.\""
#message 21 "Dispatch: \"Your call is the break-in at Hale's Pharmacy on Main Street. Reporting party is Marty Voss, Quickline Delivery. He's waiting by his van.\""
#message 22 "A department camera loaded with fresh film."
#message 23 "Prakash raises one hand without looking up. \"Save the film for evidence.\""
#message 24 "You don't have a camera."
#message 25 "Prakash puts a hand on it. \"Assignment first, Reyes.\""
#message 26 "The camera is already on your belt."
#message 27 "\"I issued that badge, Reyes. I know what it looks like.\""
#message 28 "A long counter. Prakash's side holds a rubber stamp, a coffee mug, the base radio and three wire trays."
#message 29 "A wooden bench for visitors. Someone has carved INNOCENT into the armrest."
#message 30 "Glass doors open onto Main Street to the east."
#message 31 "A hallway to the west leads to the records office."
#message 32 "Officer Dana Reyes: navy uniform, cap and duty belt. Badge 417. First week."
#message 33 "Prakash calls after you. \"Reyes! You don't have an assignment yet.\""
#message 34 "There's nothing to report yet. The case is still open."
#message 35 "You take a blank arrest report from the IN tray and fill it out at the end of the counter: the driver's log, the scene, the records, the warehouse and the arrest."
#message 36 "The report is already written."
#message 37 "You don't have a report to give him."
#message 38 "Prakash turns to the last page and taps an empty line. \"Box twelve. Arresting officer's signature.\" He slides it back."
#message 39 "You sign box twelve."
#message 40 "There's nothing to sign."
#message 41 "It's already signed."
#message 42 "\"Where's the driver's logbook? The whole case hangs on his timeline. Go get it.\" He hands the report back."
#message 43 "\"Where's the pill bottle from the scene? No physical evidence, no case.\" He hands the report back."
#message 44 "\"No scene photographs. Go back to Hale's with that camera.\" He hands the report back."
#message 45 "\"You say the warehouse ties to the Voss brothers. Show me the ledger page from records.\" He hands the report back."
#message 46 "Prakash reads every page. He checks the logbook against the ledger page, holds the pill bottle up to the light and flips through the photographs."
#message 47 "\"Timeline, evidence, records, signature.\" He stamps the report and drops it in the OUT tray. \"It'll stick. Good work, Reyes.\""
#message 48 "At 6:04 p.m. Officer Dana Reyes clocks out. Her first case is closed, and the paperwork is in the right tray."
#message 49 "\"It's filed. Go home, Reyes.\""
#message 50 "A department camera sits on the counter next to Prakash's stamp."
#message 51 "\"Bukowski's out at the patrol car on Main Street. You'll hear him before you see him.\""
#message 52 "Prakash nods without looking up. \"Reyes.\""
#message 53 "Nothing here needs photographing."
#message 55 "The clock says a few minutes before eight. It has run four minutes fast for years."
#message 56 "A potted fern. Somebody waters it with cold coffee."
#message 57 "Prakash's mug reads WORLD'S OKAYEST SERGEANT."
#message 58 "The Millhaven Police seal: a gold badge over a blue banner."
#message 60 "There's nothing here you need to take."
#message 61 "\"Marty Voss. Drives for Quickline Delivery. Very helpful on the phone. Maybe too helpful.\""
#message 62 "\"Hale's Pharmacy, down Main Street. The pharmacist is Ruth Okafor. She's been jumpy lately, and not just since last night.\""
#message 63 "\"Pier Road is nothing but warehouses. Find out which one before you go knocking.\""
#message 64 "\"Warehouse 7. You radio dispatch for backup before you go in. Bukowski will tell you the same thing.\""
#message 65 "You'd rather stand. It's your first week."
#message 66 "You flash your badge. Nobody here is impressed."
#message 67 "Arrest report, Millhaven PD. It still needs your signature in box twelve."
#message 68 "Arrest report, signed. The evidence goes with it."
#message 69 "Prakash glances up. \"Talk to me, read the board or get moving, Reyes.\""
#message 70 "WANTED: a man who steals garden gnomes. WANTED: players for the department softball team. Both have been up since spring."
#message 71 "Dispatch: \"Backup for what, Reyes? You're standing in the station.\""
#message 72 "The glass doors swing both ways. Walk through them to reach Main Street."
#message 73 "Fluorescent tubes hum overhead and turn everything faintly green."
#message 74 "A rubber stamp that says RECEIVED. Prakash uses it on everything."
#message 75 "Prakash waves you over. \"Talk to me first, Reyes.\""
#message 76 "\"Quickline Delivery. Half the shops on Main Street use them. Their drivers know every back door in town.\""
#message 77 "Blank forms fill the IN tray. You'll need one when there's something to report."
#message 78 "You reach for the OUT tray. Prakash takes the report out of your hand first. \"Not in a tray, Reyes. To me.\""
#message 79 "You don't see that here."
#message 80 "Prakash's stamp stays with Prakash."

